{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-183811",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/1b3a9a3891150ae0b187c79e2305d391f719898a9efe42b42e7bf0777d965aa3.png)\n\nFor a random variable $Z\u223cN(0,1)$ we have the following symmetry property for $a>0:$\n\n$$\nP(Z>-a)=P(Z<a)=\u03a6(a)\n$$\n\nWe're given that $Z\u223cN(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(Z<1.65).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/fd2f95626ff0a8f1aa59e94e18fddaae63216ee5962f4b7264ea952db76619b6.png)\n\nBy symmetry, this equals the area corresponding to the probability $P(Z>-1.65).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/94dfdaf777193a2a4b39e7e13c1297c3497c3d4dd474599a16a1bd4f559602b0.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z<1.65) & =P(Z>-1.65) \\\\  & =1-P(Z<-1.65) \\\\  & =1-\u03a6(-1.65) \\\\  & =1-0.0495 \\\\  & =0.9505.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
